          <change when="2024-01-19T07:58:35-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Mike%20Sampson">Vote - AcceptText - I agree that epsilon is better than eta for the infinitive in line 4, so the proposal seems right to me (but dot the iota, too). In line 7, I follow the proposed infinitive and can even make out the alpha-iota termination, but the space for theta is really quite narrow. After the infinitive's iota there is a sigma and traces of 3-4 letters. I also agree with the proposal for line 9. Finalizer: insert a paragraphos or wavy line after line 12, indent line 13, and regularize in line 11.</change>
